  long on fat and strengthens muscles and tendons.\n\nRun: 1 h 30 min in Z2
  (115–165 bpm · 4:33 min/km or slower)\n\nEasy all the way\, rather too
  slow than too fast. Bring a drink on runs over an hour.
CATEGORIES:Training
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:demo-2703-mon@lopanalys
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
DTSTART:20270118T180000
DTEND:20270118T183500
SUMMARY:Recovery jog · 35 min
DESCRIPTION:Helps the body absorb yesterday's session. You should feel bett
 er after than before.\n\nRun: 35 min in Z2 (115–165 bpm · 4:33 min/km o
 r slower)\n\nShort and very easy\, in the lower part of zone 2. If the leg
 s feel heavy: shorten the run or walk.
CATEGORIES:Training
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:demo-2703-tue@lopanalys
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
DTSTART:20270119T180000
DTEND:20270119T190500
SUMMARY:Threshold intervals · 1 h 5 min
DESCRIPTION:Moves the threshold up: you can hold a higher pace for longer.\
 n\nWarm-up: 15 min in Z2 (115–165 bpm · 4:33 min/km or slower)\nInterva
 ls: 3 × 12 min in Z4 (170–174 bpm · 4:21–4:10 min/km)\, rest 2 min\n
 Cool-down: 10 min in Z2 (115–165 bpm · 4:33 min/km or slower)\n\nJust b
 elow the threshold\, hard but controlled. You should be able to say a few 
 words and manage one more interval when you finish. Jog or walk in the res
 ts.
CATEGORIES:Training
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:demo-2703-thu@lopanalys
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
DTSTART:20270121T180000
DTEND:20270121T184800
SUMMARY:Fartlek · 48 min
DESCRIPTION:Speed in a playful form: gets the body used to threshold pace w
 ithout the wear of intervals.\n\nWarm-up: 10 min in Z2 (115–165 bpm · 4
 :33 min/km or slower)\nIntervals: 6 × 3 min in Z4 (170–174 bpm · 4:21
 –4:10 min/km)\, easy jog 2 min between\nCool-down: 10 min in Z2 (115–1
 65 bpm · 4:33 min/km or slower)\n\nPick up to threshold effort in the sur
 ges and jog easily between them without stopping.
CATEGORIES:Training
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:demo-2703-sat@lopanalys
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
DTSTART:20270123T090000
DTEND:20270123T095000
SUMMARY:Easy run · 50 min
DESCRIPTION:Builds endurance without wearing you down. Most of the training
  should look like this.\n\nRun: 50 min in Z2 (115–165 bpm · 4:33 min/km
  or slower)\n\nEven\, easy pace at which you can talk in full sentences. I
 f the heart rate passes zone 2 on a hill: slow down or walk.
CATEGORIES:Training
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
